1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
EcoGenesis V2 is the evidence-bounded release of the

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:07,000
Barcode-to-GBIF Evidence Compiler. It addresses a fragmented

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,500
evidence problem: occurrence records may live in one system,

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:14,000
DNA barcode fragments in another, BLAST or Sequence ID tables

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,500
in a lab pipeline, and publication metadata in spreadsheets.

6
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:21,000
When these pieces are not connected, useful evidence can be

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,500
lost, and species-level claims can become stronger than the

8
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:28,000
data actually support.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,500
EcoGenesis is a Barcode-to-GBIF Evidence Compiler. It takes

10
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:35,000
DNA barcode, metabarcoding, Sequence ID and BLAST-like

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,500
outputs, then runs configured evidence gates. The result is

12
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:42,000
not species truth. It is a bounded rank result, a

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,500
publication-readiness check, a repair plan, and a reproducible

14
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:49,000
Evidence Pack for review.

15
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,667
On the public demo site, judges can open the overview, run the

16
00:00:52,667 --> 00:00:56,333
compiler, inspect the Evidence Map, view the Fragment Graph,

17
00:00:56,333 --> 00:01:00,000
open Regression and Audits, read Methods and Audits, and

18
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,667
download the GBIF Repair Pack. A persistent prototype notice

19
00:01:03,667 --> 00:01:07,333
states that the tool is not an independently validated

20
00:01:07,333 --> 00:01:11,000
taxonomic identifier or a GBIF publisher.

21
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,667
The Run Compiler screen is where molecular evidence enters the

22
00:01:14,667 --> 00:01:18,333
system. A user can upload a CSV, start from a demo workflow,

23
00:01:18,333 --> 00:01:22,000
or test a reference fragment. The compiler checks required

24
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,667
molecular fields, sequence context, reference-hit metrics,

25
00:01:25,667 --> 00:01:29,333
reference and sequence-quality evidence, and publication

26
00:01:29,333 --> 00:01:33,000
metadata before it routes a record.

27
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Under the current fail-closed reference attestation, the

28
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,000
bundled mixed demo emits no species rule-pass. AALB-COI-good

29
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,000
and AALB-COI-metadata-gap are ambiguous, AALB-COI-ambiguous is

30
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:49,000
bounded at genus, and AALB-COI-short is weak. The metadata-gap

31
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:53,000
row also carries publication blockers. These are run-local

32
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:57,000
rule results and validation candidates, not independently

33
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:01,000
confirmed identifications or accepted GBIF records.

34
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,333
The Evidence Map shows hashed GBIF occurrence context beside

35
00:02:04,333 --> 00:02:07,667
molecular rule-evidence rows, graph objects and export

36
00:02:07,667 --> 00:02:11,000
boundaries. The occurrence rows are explicitly unlinked from

37
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,333
the molecular rows unless shared specimen or event identifiers

38
00:02:14,333 --> 00:02:17,667
are supplied. The map cannot upgrade a molecular claim and is

39
00:02:17,667 --> 00:02:21,000
not evidence of presence by itself.

40
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,500
In the Evidence Map, reviewers can see rule-supported

41
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:28,000
candidates, repair-required rows, review-only hypotheses and

42
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,500
blocked exports. The same view exposes release checks, graph

43
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:35,000
audits and export boundaries before download. Passing those

44
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,500
checks means the files agree for that run; it does not

45
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:42,000
establish external scientific validity.

46
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,167
The Fragment Graph shows how marker fragments link to

47
00:02:45,167 --> 00:02:48,333
reference taxa and an LCA-bounded rank. When a fragment points

48
00:02:48,333 --> 00:02:51,500
to multiple close taxa, EcoGenesis reports the most specific

49
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:54,667
rank allowed by the configured rules instead of forcing a

50
00:02:54,667 --> 00:02:57,833
species claim. Evidence, competitors and caveats remain

51
00:02:57,833 --> 00:03:01,000
together.

52
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:04,667
Uncertainty is handled through explicit gates: identity and

53
00:03:04,667 --> 00:03:08,333
coverage, ambiguity and LCA downgrade, barcode gap, locally

54
00:03:08,333 --> 00:03:12,000
unique k-mer support in the selected reference set, marker

55
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,667
profile, publication checks and graph provenance. A top hit

56
00:03:15,667 --> 00:03:19,333
does not become a species-level validation candidate unless

57
00:03:19,333 --> 00:03:23,000
every configured requirement passes.

58
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,667
Regression and integrity checks are built into the submission

59
00:03:26,667 --> 00:03:30,333
package. The project includes backend and frontend tests,

60
00:03:30,333 --> 00:03:34,000
repeated-fixture competition batches, adversarial cases, graph

61
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,667
audits and contest-readiness checks. They test fail-closed

62
00:03:37,667 --> 00:03:41,333
behavior and internal consistency; independent multi-taxon

63
00:03:41,333 --> 00:03:45,000
scientific validation remains future work.

64
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,667
The final deliverable is the Evidence Pack. It includes CSV,

65
00:03:48,667 --> 00:03:52,333
JSON, HTML, rule-evidence, graph and audit outputs for review,

66
00:03:52,333 --> 00:03:56,000
repair and reuse. Researchers can inspect sequence decision

67
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,667
tables, blockers, validation-candidate templates, molecular

68
00:03:59,667 --> 00:04:03,333
evidence reports, graph provenance and machine-readable

69
00:04:03,333 --> 00:04:07,000
artifacts.

70
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,571
EcoGenesis is a working contest prototype with a live demo,

71
00:04:10,571 --> 00:04:14,143
public source code, reproducible run-local outputs and

72
00:04:14,143 --> 00:04:17,714
downloadable evidence artifacts. It is not yet a validated

73
00:04:17,714 --> 00:04:21,286
scientific identifier or complete GBIF publishing pipeline.

74
00:04:21,286 --> 00:04:24,857
The call to action is simple: run the workflow, inspect its

75
00:04:24,857 --> 00:04:28,429
boundaries, and validate candidate records externally before

76
00:04:28,429 --> 00:04:32,000
publication.
